load("@komira//tools/build/mojo:defs.bzl", "mojo_library")

# The mutable data-graph store and its ingest, parts 1 to 7 (the second of the
# packages in docs/design/knowledge_graph_port.md): bi-temporal edges (a replaced
# fact is closed, not erased), entity resolution (name similarity, the dedup
# cascade and a directed alias map), the source facet with its tombstone set, the
# model seams (Embedder, Extractor, LlmClient, each with a stub), the rule-driven
# extractor (a rule set is host data), the source cursor store and the
# in-memory working set that loads a snapshot or a delta chain and writes back a
# base or a delta, erasure of a partition, the warm cache, compaction and
# embedding top-k and the episode ingest path (extract with a bounded gleaning
# loop, resolve entities, apply bi-temporal edges, store a base or a delta), the
# structured path (known facts without extraction, a source that replaces its
# facts, an ended fact) and the SurfaceAdapter seam. It depends on
# komira_kg_format (for the open-interval marker), komira_json (for the facet's
# attrs JSON) and komira_objectstore (the cursor store rides its conditional-write
# trait), and on their closure; it reads no clock and no environment, and calls no
# model: a judgment is a trait the caller implements.
#
# The welded tests: test_bitemporal closes an overlapping edge and keeps its
# row, and answers "what held at E" and "what was believed at S about E";
# test_name_similarity pins normalization, entropy and the signature values;
# test_dedup runs the cascade on stated inputs, with a scripted judge;
# test_alias_map checks that resolution is stable under reordering;
# test_source_facet round-trips the facet and keys the tombstone set by source
# and facet; test_embedder pins the reported dimension, the vector width against
# unpack_embedding_checked and the stub's stated components; test_extractor and
# test_llm_client check that the stubs satisfy their traits, answer from their
# tables, and end a gleaning loop; test_rule_pattern pins the whole-token pattern
# language and its refusals, test_rule_scan what each kind of rule finds,
# test_rule_extractor fixed entities and triples for stated rule sets (two sets
# give two vocabularies) and the gleaning contract; test_cursor_codec the stored
# form of a cursor and the truncated, trailing, oversize and non-UTF-8 bodies it
# refuses; test_cursor_store write-read, a conflicting writer, bounded retries
# and store failures; test_working_set_roundtrip writes a working set as a base
# snapshot and reads it back field for field (at two embedding dimensions, with
# NUL bytes in the text), pins one consistent set of tables per snapshot and
# deterministic objects; test_working_set_delta merges a base and deltas to the
# rows of a full rewrite and checks what a delta carries; test_working_set_refusals
# refuses a wrong embedding dimension against the manifest and malformed tables;
# test_working_set_commit narrows a committed set's vectors to what a reload holds
# and re-baselines its diff; test_compaction folds a chain to the rows it merged
# to, keeps a pinned chain and its objects, stamps retired deltas, carries a
# delta appended meanwhile and refuses a second fold of a replaced head;
# test_erase removes one partition's rows, edges, closures, names and embeddings
# from the head and keeps the others; test_erase_race erases the rows a writer
# slipped in during the erasure and keeps its other rows; test_rewrite_repair
# finishes a fold or an erasure that stopped after its commit and orders a
# writer's delta before the bootstrap; test_warm_cache keys the resident merge by
# the head and lends it read-only; test_embedding_topk ranks by cosine with ties
# by node id (against a full sort), skips a non-finite stored row and refuses
# k <= 0, a wrong or non-finite query and a wrong cell; test_ingest_gleaning folds
# gleaning passes, stops on a pass with nothing new and seeds the model with the
# known entities; test_ingest_resolve resolves mentions to existing, judged or new
# entities, per partition and within the candidate count; test_ingest_edges
# resolves endpoints, dates undated triples, closes a contradicted edge and adds
# no repeat of a live one; test_ingest_episode ingests an episode to its nodes,
# edges and provenance, skips an unchanged body, appends deltas from a resident
# set and writes a full base when a delta cannot say a closure; test_ingest_failure
# refuses a wrong embedding dimension, a knob out of range and a set a delta
# cannot carry, and leaves the store unchanged when the model or the embedder
# fails; test_ingest_structured ingests known facts without the extractor, skips
# an unchanged extraction by its fingerprint, supersedes a judged contradiction,
# stores an end time and refuses an empty interval, and leaves the store unchanged
# when the embedder or a judge fails; test_ingest_source_diff closes exactly the
# edges a source no longer states (not another source's, partition's or untagged
# ingest's), applies only the changed facts of a re-ingest and keeps an ended
# fact's end; test_surface_adapter lowers made-up records to the expected
# episodes with their text verbatim.
mojo_library(
